**Given:**

Amount (A) = ₹2160

Time (t) = 3 years

Rate of Interest (r) = 20% per annum

**Formula used:**

A = P + SI

SI = dfrac{P times r times t}{100}

**Calculation:**

2160 = P + dfrac{P times 20 times 3}{100}

⇒ 2160 = P + dfrac{60P}{100}

⇒ 2160 = P + 0.6P

⇒ 2160 = 1.6P

⇒ P = dfrac{2160}{1.6}

⇒ P = ₹1350

**Simple Interest for 1 year:**

SI = dfrac{P times r times t}{100}

SI = dfrac{1350 times 20 times 1}{100}

⇒ SI = ₹270

**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**

